{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgthTNPYSZfSrmJm3iuT9","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The direct effect of MLP neurons on the copy is negligible. Summed over all 3,584 neurons, no layer from 8 to 23 contributes more than about 0.06 logits to the copy margin, either at the loop's first cycle or in late cycles, and the largest single-neuron change is 0.009. The confident copying (log-odds around 6 by cycle 3) must therefore come from the token-mixing blocks: full attention and the Gated DeltaNet layers. That fits the classic induction-copy picture of loops, and it means the mid-layer repetition neurons could act only indirectly. To locate the copy signal, I will decompose each layer's write to the residual stream, recorded in pass 2, into its mixer part (layer write minus the MLP's own output) and its MLP part. I will then project both onto the same copy-margin direction for cycle 0, late cycles and ordinary pre-loop text. The mixer layers whose copy contribution jumps from pre-loop to late-loop are where loop-sustaining copying happens.\n\n```python\n# Hypothesis: the copy margin in loops is carried by a few token-mixer blocks (full-attn and/or GatedDeltaNet), growing from cycle0 to late cycles.\nout = []\nHprev = np.load('/work/fwd_5/hidden_0.npy', mmap_mode='r')\nfor l in range(24):\n    Hn = np.load(f'/work/fwd_5/hidden_{l+1}.npy', mmap_mode='r')\n    Wd_l = load_original(f'model.language_model.layers.{l}.mlp.down_proj.weight').numpy(); Aact = np.load(f'/work/fwd_5/mlp_act_{l}.npy', mmap_mode='r')\n    acc_ = np.zeros((2, 3))\n    for t in range(2):\n        T_ = lens5[t] - 1; dl = np.asarray(Hn[t, :T_], np.float32) - np.asarray(Hprev[t, :T_], np.float32)\n        mlp_o = np.asarray(Aact[t, :T_], np.float32) @ Wd_l.T; mix_o = dl - mlp_o\n        cm = (mix_o * dirs5[t]).sum(1); cl = (mlp_o * dirs5[t]).sum(1)\n        m0, m3 = cyc_masks(t); pre = np.zeros(T_, bool); pre[100:on5[t] - 1] = True\n        acc_[0] += [cm[pre].mean()/2, cm[m0].mean()/2, cm[m3].mean()/2]; acc_[1] += [cl[pre].mean()/2, cl[m0].mean()/2, cl[m3].mean()/2]\n    out.append((l, 'A' if l in (3, 7, 11, 15, 19, 23) else 'D', *np.round(acc_[0], 2), *np.round(acc_[1], 2)))\n    Hprev = Hn\nOD = pd.DataFrame(out, columns=['layer', 'type', 'mix_pre', 'mix_c0', 'mix_late', 'mlp_pre', 'mlp_c0', 'mlp_late'])\nprint(OD.to_string()); print('sum', OD[['mix_pre', 'mix_c0', 'mix_late', 'mlp_pre', 'mlp_c0', 'mlp_late']].sum().round(2).to_dict())\n```"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":7882,"cache_read_input_tokens":51031,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":7882},"output_tokens":5,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b4bcd242-3053-49df-a015-76e7a59477b0","uuid":"b9d79177-a63c-4260-9a64-fe4f76a56fcf","timestamp":"2026-11-10T05:31:06.502Z","request_id":"req_011CgthTMzUKyKGxmyzjgkBc"}
